Package: balancesample
Title: Multivariate Balanced Data Splitting for 'rsample'
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Jeffrey M.", "Girard", , "jeffgirard@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-7359-3746"))
Description: Creates training/testing splits, training/validation/testing
    splits, and cross-validation folds that are balanced on several
    variables at once. Numeric and categorical variables are balanced with
    anticlustering as in Papenberg and Klau (2021)
    <doi:10.1037/met0000301> and Papenberg (2024)
    <doi:10.1111/bmsp.12315>, data twinning as in Vakayil and Joseph
    (2022) <doi:10.1002/sam.11574>, rerandomization as in Morgan and Rubin
    (2012) <doi:10.1214/12-AOS1008>, or crossed strata. Categorical
    variables can also be stratified exactly, and rows from the same group
    can be kept together. Results are 'rsample' objects for resampling and
    tuning with 'tune'.
